<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple Computer//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  MobileSubstrate filter for icanhasrez.dylib. ONE process, and it is not the
  one you would guess.

  backboardd is the render server -- its LaunchDaemon
  (/System/Library/LaunchDaemons/com.apple.backboardd.plist) vends
  com.apple.CARenderServer among its MachServices -- and the display mode list
  is enumerated there. That is measured, not assumed: an earlier build hooked
  the same QuartzCore function inside com.apple.lowtide, logged a clean
  install with a matching prologue signature, and then never fired once,
  because lowtide's CADisplay receives an already-built list over IPC.

  Executables rather than Bundles because backboardd is a plain executable at
  /usr/libexec/backboardd with no bundle identifier to match on. lowtide is
  deliberately NOT here: nothing in this tweak is of any use in the UI
  process, and every additional process a dylib is injected into is
  additional risk for no return.

  DO NOT WIDEN THIS. backboardd crashing takes the whole display stack down,
  which is a strictly worse failure than lowtide crashing. What makes it
  acceptable at all is the dylib's own discipline: it verifies a 16-byte
  prologue signature before touching anything, writes the display's
  native-size fields only when they are empty, and never accepts a resolution
  other than the one the attached display's own EDID asks for. Deleting this
  plist over SSH disables everything, and is the recovery path.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Filter</key>
    <dict>
        <key>Executables</key>
        <array>
            <string>backboardd</string>
        </array>
    </dict>
</dict>
</plist>
